From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oliver Sargison <sargo@sargo.cc>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 22:09:53 +1300
Subject: [PATCH 80/87] Plutonium: the native window cross-fade runs on the
 compositor thread

The old frame's opacity was stepped from the main thread each frame, so
a busy shell page made the fade stutter. Fade it with a cc opacity
animation on its effect node instead (as LinkHighlightImpl does). The
main thread drops the frame when the animation finishes, or when it
should have. A resize during the fade holds the frame where it had got
to. Without threaded animation it is stepped as before.
---
